module fluorescence

manifest rt_qpcr_mix
manifest gapdh_primers_probes
manifest f127_solution
manifest target_rna
manifest nuclease_free_water

instructions:

// Step 1: Assemble the 20 uL ddPCR reaction mix (Luna Probe One-Step RT-qPCR 4X Mix,
// human GAPDH primers/probes, 10 w/v% F127 co-surfactant to prevent droplet coalescence,
// diluted human control RNA target, and nuclease-free water to volume)
qpcr_mix = dispense 5 units of rt_qpcr_mix
primers = dispense 1 units of gapdh_primers_probes
f127 = dispense 2 units of f127_solution
target = dispense 10 units of target_rna
water = dispense 2 units of nuclease_free_water

combined1 = mix qpcr_mix with primers
combined2 = mix combined1 with f127
combined3 = mix combined2 with target
reaction = mix combined3 with water

// Note: pipette-based droplet generation into fluorinated oil (elliptical-tip pinch-off into
// a PCR tube) has no distinct BioScript droplet-generation primitive beyond the dispense/mix
// above, and is not separately modeled.

// Step 2: Reverse transcription
heat reaction at 52c for 600s

// Step 3: Initial denaturation
heat reaction at 95c for 120s

// Step 4: PCR amplification -- 40 thermal cycles (denature / anneal-extend)
repeat 40 times {
    heat reaction at 95c for 10s
    heat reaction at 60c for 30s
}

// Step 5: Post-PCR fluorescence imaging of droplets to count FAM-positive (amplified) droplets
fam_signal = detect fluorescence on reaction for 5s

dispose reaction
